# Party banter around Old Bonegrinder. Each node opens with an `if` gate: the node is eligible only while its
# condition holds. Party members speak only through interjections; a line plays if a matching member is present.

~ banter_sails
if not flag.morgantha_home_met and not flag.bonegrinder_burned
interject tag:curious: A windmill with the sails tied down, and the chimney going full blast. What's it grinding, if the wind isn't turning it?
interject tag:blunt: Don't answer that.
if tag:blunt
interject class:wizard: I wasn't going to. I was going to think it very loudly.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_keeper
if flag.ilinca_met and not flag.children_rescued
interject class:cleric: Lycanthropes who worship nothing but keeping watch. I was taught they were all cursed. She seems more tired than cursed.
interject tag:loyal: Most people who keep a watch are both.
endif
-> END

~ banter_coven
if flag.coven_explained and not flag.morgantha_slain and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:ratatoille
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Right then. We don't fight three hags. We fight one hag, three times.
interject name:ratatoille: That is, technically, correct. Split a coven and its magic curdles, like a sauce pulled off the heat too soon.
endif
-> END

~ banter_pastry_taste
if flag.dream_pastry_eaten and flag.offalia_met and name:thistle and name:ratatoille
interject name:thistle: I ate one of those in the village. Best thing I ever ate. Better than yours, Cook. Sorry.
interject name:ratatoille: Thistle. Think what the flour is ground from.
interject name:thistle: ...Oh.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bella_pact
if flag.bella_pact and not flag.morgantha_slain
interject tag:pious: We've promised a mill full of stolen souls to a hag so that she'll sit out a fight. I keep turning it over to find the side that looks better.
interject tag:blunt: There isn't one. There's the side with the children on it. That'll have to do.
endif
-> END

~ banter_children_out
if flag.children_rescued and name:kip_smudgewick and name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Two of them, alive, walking down a hill on their own feet. I gave them an apricot each. No obligation.
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Toma waved at me. I waved back, a big one. He sat down in the mud, laughing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_the_truth
if flag.sarnov_truth_told and name:godrick_pendlebrook and name:liriel_dawnsong
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: We told a little girl her mother sold her. I keep thinking we ought to have lied.
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: She asked us. A lie would have been one more thing taken from her, and she'd have known it.
endif
-> END

~ banter_home_again
if flag.bonegrinder_children_fate == "home"
interject tag:curious: Do you think their mother will buy pastries again?
interject tag:blunt: I think she'll look at every child in the village for the rest of her life. That's not a punishment I'd wish on anyone. She earned it anyway.
endif
-> END

~ banter_bargain
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "gold" or flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "truce"
interject tag:blunt: We paid a hag to give back children she stole, and walked out past her oven. Somebody tell me that was the clever thing.
if tag:blunt
interject class:wizard: It was the living thing. Clever comes second, in this valley.
endif
endif
-> END

~ banter_dream_debt
if flag.bonegrinder_bargain == "dream" and not flag.morgantha_slain
interject tag:curious: The one she took a dream from. Do you know what it was?
interject tag:pious: No. That's the part I can't forgive her. Not the taking. That I don't know what's missing.
endif
-> END

~ banter_another_house
if flag.death_house_children_met and flag.sarnov_children_met and name:thistle and name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:thistle: Another stone box with children shut in the top. Is that how town folk build them? On purpose?
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Not the builders, love. The landlord.
endif
-> END

~ banter_kesten
if flag.bone_heap_searched
interject class:cleric: Brother Kesten came up this hill alone with a cudgel and a prayer. I'll wear his symbol a while, so that someone finishes the walk.
endif
-> END

~ banter_keepers
if flag.ilinca_vouched
interject tag:curious: Raven-eyed innkeeper in Vallaki. She meant Urwin, didn't she? The whole family's birds, I'd bet.
interject tag:loyal: Then that's a family that owes us. Good to have, in a place like this.
endif
-> END

~ banter_trade_ended
if flag.pastry_trade == "ended" and name:wren_featherfoot and name:kip_smudgewick
interject name:wren_featherfoot: No more dream pastries anywhere in the valley. A lot of folk are going to wake up tomorrow and remember they're sad.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: Better sad than eaten. Sad folk bolt their doors. Dreamers leave them on the latch.
endif
-> END

~ banter_ireena_mill
if guest:ireena and flag.morgantha_home_met
interject guest:ireena: My father bought one of her baskets once, the winter he couldn't sleep. He slept all the next day, smiling. I thought she'd done him a kindness.
interject tag:pious: It was a kindness, from him. Not from her.
endif
-> END
